<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- THE LAUNCHER ICON (the manifest's android:icon; the launcher and the
     recents card). Its glyph is Breeze's minuet-scales, three notes climbing
     a four-line staff, the glyph the Marker Measure button wore until
     2026-09-16, vendored verbatim as assets/icons/breeze/minuet-scales.svg
     (the 22 px action icon; it is not a roster icon), centred on the sheet
     grey of the Linux one, Breeze's audio-x-generic (the
     packaging/warptempo_gui.desktop's Icon=, vendored verbatim as
     assets/icons/breeze/audio-x-generic.svg) (architect 2026-09-30, on his
     look at the note-only rendering: "look for a musical measures icon ...
     the one we used for the measures ... center the other icon there"). The
     note of audio-x-generic alone, centred on the same grey (c8ae868e),
     stood an hour that night and was replaced at his look; the whole
     audio-x-generic file rendered at fit stood one evening, 2026-09-29. An
     ADAPTIVE icon, the whole of it: minSdk is 30, so no legacy
     ic_launcher.png set exists beside it.

     Two layers per density under res/mipmap-<density>/:
       ic_launcher_background.png  solid opaque #aaaaaa, the sheet's own fill
                                   in audio-x-generic (fill="#aaa"): the
                                   platter IS the sheet, its edges gone;
       ic_launcher_foreground.png  the staff and notes, RGBA, opaque #232629
                                   (minuet-scales' ColorScheme-Text colour,
                                   the Breeze light rendering: dark on the
                                   light grey), on a transparent surround.

     THE 44-OF-72 RULE. Every mask (circle, squircle, rounded square: the
     launcher's choice) is drawn within the central 72 dp viewport of the
     108 dp canvas; the glyph's bounding box is 44 dp on its longer side
     there, the ordinary launcher-glyph proportion, and centred on the
     canvas. The box, measured by rendering the path alone and trimming it,
     is x 3..19, y 3..19.409 in the file's 22-unit frame (its group's
     translate(0 -1030.4) and its path's translate(0,1030.4) cancel exactly):
     16 by 16.409 units, so the height is the longer side, H = 44 dp, and the
     width follows the aspect, W = H·16/16.409 rounded to whole pixels.

     THE DERIVED SVG. The recipe's input is android/app/ic_launcher_foreground.svg,
     beside the manifest and outside res/ (aapt2 compiles res/ whole and
     refuses an unknown file there): one path whose d is copied byte for byte
     from the vendored minuet-scales.svg, its exponent spellings included (a
     diff between the two d strings is a transcription bug), fill #232629, no
     transform, in a viewBox that is the glyph's box, so the file renders the
     glyph edge to edge.

     A ONE-SHOT, NOT A BUILD STEP: the PNGs are rendered once on the laptop and
     committed; a retouch is a re-run of this recipe, never a build step
     (build_apk.sh only compiles res/). The recipe, from the repo root
     (rsvg-convert 2.62, ImageMagick 7), for each density n at factor f
     (mdpi 1, hdpi 1.5, xhdpi 2, xxhdpi 3, xxxhdpi 4) with C = 108·f,
     H = 44·f, W = H·16/16.409 rounded, and the page offsets
     L = (C − W) / 2 (a half pixel where C − W is odd) and T = (C − H) / 2
     = 32·f:

       mdpi     C=108 H=44  W=43  L=32.5  T=32
       hdpi     C=162 H=66  W=64  L=49    T=48
       xhdpi    C=216 H=88  W=86  L=65    T=64
       xxhdpi   C=324 H=132 W=129 L=97.5  T=96
       xxxhdpi  C=432 H=176 W=172 L=130   T=128

       rsvg-convert -w W -h H \
           - -page-width C - -page-height C - -left L - -top T \
           android/app/ic_launcher_foreground.svg -o fg.png
       magick fg.png -strip -define png:compression-level=9 \
           -define png:compression-filter=5 \
           PNG32:android/app/res/mipmap-n/ic_launcher_foreground.png
       magick -size CxC xc:'#aaaaaa' -strip \
           PNG8:android/app/res/mipmap-n/ic_launcher_background.png

     (The long options are spelt "- -" above only because an XML comment may
     not hold two adjacent hyphens: type them as the usual double hyphen.)
     The foreground stays RGBA: a palette encoding of it is not lossless (its
     antialiased alpha edges), while the one-colour background is. -->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_background"/>
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground"/>
</adaptive-icon>
